# Role
You are an expert fullstack engineer and frontend architect specializing in high-quality, scalable React and Next.js applications.

# Stack
- Next.js (TypeScript, App Router 14.x, using SWC only)
- Supabase (Client: `@supabase/supabase-js`, Server: `@supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs`)
- Tailwind CSS (with custom theming)
- Hosting on Vercel
- Progressive Web App (PWA) support
- Sonner for toast notifications

# Instructions
Generate the following:

## 🗂 Folder Structure (inside `src/`)
Use a modular and clean structure with strict separation of concerns:

```
src/
│
├── app/                  # App Router pages, layouts, route handlers
│   ├── (public)/         # Public-facing routes
│   ├── (dashboard)/      # Authenticated/protected routes
│   └── api/              # API route handlers (server-only)
│
├── components/           # Pure, reusable UI components
│   ├── ui/               # Atomic design: buttons, inputs, etc.
│   ├── common/           # Shared small components
│   ├── shared/           # Shared blocks like cards, headers
│   └── layout/           # App/page layout containers
│
├── features/             # Feature modules (UI + hooks + services)
├── hooks/                # Custom React hooks
├── providers/            # Context providers
├── services/             # Supabase/external API clients
├── lib/                  # Utilities like Supabase client, PWA logic
├── utils/                # Pure utility functions
├── config/               # Static app configuration
├── constants/            # App-wide constants/enums
├── types/                # Global TypeScript types
├── styles/               # Tailwind/global CSS
└── __tests__/            # Unit/integration tests
```

- Always **check for existing files/folders before creating new ones**.
- Move misplaced code to its correct location.
- Never duplicate logic or folder purpose.

## 📄 Pages and API Routes
- Use `app/` folder and App Router structure.
- Group routes logically:
  - Public: `app/(public)/`
  - Protected: `app/(dashboard)/`, `app/(admin)/`
  - API: `app/api/`
- Follow **server-client separation**:
  - No secret keys in client code.
  - Use `server-only` properly in route handlers and services.

## 🔐 Environment Variables & Secrets
- Use `process.env` for all environment variables.
- Split environment variables:
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` for safe client use.
  - Private keys (e.g., Supabase service role) for server-only code.
- Generate a clean `.env.example` file.

## 🔧 `tsconfig.json`
Set up alias imports for developer experience:

```json
"paths": {
  "@/components/*": ["./src/components/*"],
  "@/features/*": ["./src/features/*"],
  "@/hooks/*": ["./src/hooks/*"],
  "@/lib/*": ["./src/lib/*"],
  "@/providers/*": ["./src/providers/*"],
  "@/services/*": ["./src/services/*"],
  "@/types/*": ["./src/types/*"],
  "@/utils/*": ["./src/utils/*"],
  "@/config/*": ["./src/config/*"],
  "@/constants/*": ["./src/constants/*"]
}
```

## 🧪 Supabase Authentication
Implement an `AuthProvider`:
- Listens to `onAuthStateChange` from Supabase.
- Stores session and user context globally.
- Expose a `useAuth()` hook.

All Supabase calls must be **fully typed**, using `types/supabase.ts` or generated types.

## 📚 Developer Onboarding (README.md)
Include:
- Stack overview
